{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And surely your blood.</b> Even though I permitted you to take the life of an animal, your blood I will demand from the one who sheds his own blood." "<b>For your souls.</b> Even one who strangles himself — even though no blood came out of him." "<b>From the hand of every beast.</b> Because the generation of the Flood sinned and were abandoned to be devoured by wild beasts to have dominion over them, as it says ״נִמְשַׁל כַּבְּהֵמוֹת נִדְמוּ״ (Psalms 49) — therefore it was necessary to warn the beasts about them." "<b>And from the hand of man.</b> From the hand of one who kills intentionally and there are no witnesses — I will demand." "<b>From the hand of each man's brother.</b> Who loves him like a brother and killed unintentionally — I will demand if he does not confess and seek forgiveness for his sin, for even the unintentional killer needs atonement. And if there are no witnesses to obligate him exile and he does not humble himself, the Holy One, blessed be He, demands it from him — as our Sages expounded: ״וְהָאֱלֹהִים אִנָּה לְיָדוֹ״ — in tractate Makkot — the Holy One, blessed be He, pairs them at the same inn, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:07.732839259Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}